WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.534
-Our next guest has
a comedy special

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:06.601
called "Trash White"
streaming now on HBO Max.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.067
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.667
please welcome the very funny
Moses Storm.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:12.501
♪♪
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.634
-Oh!

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:16.501
Thank you so much.

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:17.701
Thank you!

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.934
Oh, my God!

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:21.400
[ Laughs ]

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.701
This is already one of the
better birthdays that I've had.

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:28.534
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:29.467
I'll explain.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:30.968
I grew up very poor.

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.400
My mom was a single parent.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.767
She had five kids.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.467
We were on food stamps.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:36.868
When we ran out of welfare,

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.234
we would actually eat
from the garbage.

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:40.734
We'd Dumpster dive.

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:43.934
And a lot of people
find it hard to believe

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:47.601
that I was ever that poor
because like look at this.

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:49.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.801
Not only do I look rich, I --

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.434
I look like I was conceived

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:56.000
at an Ivy League
a cappella concert.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:58.567 --> 00:00:59.467
♪ She be do wop ♪

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:01.901
♪ My dad owns every university ♪

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:02.801
♪ She be do wop ♪

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.367
♪ What even is adversity? ♪

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:07.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:10.367
Evil rich, like a King Joffrey,
"Game of Thrones."

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:11.901
[ Laughter ]
Like I'm only here

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.367
to bother Sophie.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:17.701
[ English accent ]
You thought you killed me,
Sansa?!

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.701
[ Applause ]

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:22.767
I hated being on food stamps
because the technical term

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:25.434
for a family on welfare
in this country

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:28.701
is a food insecure household.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.868
[ Murmuring ]
I never like that.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:34.300
Food insecure -- it just makes
a pretty serious issue

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.567
just sound adorable.

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:37.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:38.934
Almost like
the government's like,

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:40.534
"Oh, come on.

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:41.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.534
Just show us your food."

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:45.767
[ Laughter and applause ]
Show it!"

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.767
And then I'm like --

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:50.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:51.567
Mnh-mnh!

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.968
You know, I'm starving,
not bashful.

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:57.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.234
When we ran out of food stamps,
we would go to food banks

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:03.801
and, for some reason,
all of the food at food banks

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.200
was just dented cans.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:09.601
It seemed suspicious.

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.067
Are they doing that

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:12.934
or how are you guys shopping?

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.334
[ Laughter ]
Were you like, "What is this?

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.434
Low sodium corn?

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:18.534
Get outta here!

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:19.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:20.968
Not my brand!"

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:24.133
[ Applause ]

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:30.434
Oh, actually,
on my eighth birthday,

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:33.067
we were living
in this really terrible, hot,

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:35.501
awful part of Florida

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:37.067
called Florida.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:40.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:42.501
And, anytime that we wanted
to go swimming,

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:45.968
we would just break in
to a fancy condo community,

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:47.934
just so we could use their pool.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.467
And, on the way there,

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.133
we'd stop off at the grocery
store Dumpster,

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.267
like we always did,

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.567
[ Laughter ]
but it's a birthday miracle.

00:02:54.567 --> 00:02:57.033
I had never seen
anything like this.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:58.300
This grocery store threw out

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.400
their entire ice cream
department at once.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:04.701
So now, every kind of ice cream
that we could never afford

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:07.334
is now in three
large trash bags.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.434
My four siblings and I,
we waste no time.

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.133
Right there,
back of the store,

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:13.567
just start shoveling
half melted ice cream

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:15.634
into our face
as fast as possible,

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.901
like little
skin-covered raccoons,

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:20.400
[ Laughter ]
before it all melts.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.400
And I don't know
if you've ever had

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.367
to speed eat dairy in the sun...

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:29.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:32.634
...but we are not doing well.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:35.667
Have you ever been so full
that you feel it in your neck?

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.501
You know that --
[ Mutters ]

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:40.534
Every burp is so high-stakes.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:41.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:44.367
Every burp,
it's like it's a contraction

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.634
for the barf baby you're
about to deliver.

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:49.167
[ Laughter and applause ]
It has a pulse.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.534
My stomach is kicking.

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:52.033
[ Laughter ]
If I lived in Georgia right now,

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.901
it would be illegal
to throw this up.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:57.868
[ Laughter, ohs, and applause ]

00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:01.767
[Indistinct]

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:02.934
We get to this fancy pool.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.968
The one downside
of this very fancy pool

00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:08.968
is it had an infuriating
amount of security.

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:10.200
It was way too good.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.133
They had a guard shack
security guard,

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.767
a roaming security guard,

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:16.200
and just a pool security guard.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.767
Made it not fun.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.467
My mom is like,
"Okay, look at me.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:20.334
Don't worry about it.

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:21.901
Just stick with the regular plan

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:23.467
when breaking in
to one of these pools --

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:24.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.033
all of you kids spread out

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.767
as far as possible.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:31.000
One by one, you enter the pool
from different sides.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.334
When safe,
we can all meet in the middle.

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:35.767
We're not going to flash mob
people with poverty."

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:37.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.834 --> 00:04:43.000
The second that I jump in
on my side of the pool,

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.701
I know I'm going to vomit.

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:48.601
[ Laughter ]
So my plan is
to just put my mouth

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.267
under the water...
[ Ohs ]

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:51.868
...just so it won't make a sound
and then just --

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:53.968
[ Heaving ]
[ Ewws and laughter ]

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:55.367
So much.

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:59.734
It looked like I'd eaten nothing
but 700 vanilla lava lamps.

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.267
This kid with red hair, he comes
to the surface of the pool,

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:08.367
takes his goggles off and goes,
"Oh, my God!"

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:09.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:10.467
Because he had the full

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:14.033
IMAX 3-D experience below.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:15.968
That causes my older brother
Jonah,

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:18.501
who was already not doing well,

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:20.300
[ Laughter ]
he turns, he sees me,

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.868
and now, he starts vomiting
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:26.300
because vomiting is a lot
like those inspirational quotes

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.000
that white girls
will post online --

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.100
very contagious and embarrassing

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.167
when it slips out
of your mouth in public.

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:37.200
So, over here, he just starts,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.000
"If you can't handle me
at my worst,

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.767
you don't deserve me
at my best."

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:43.701
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:47.167
That triggers my two sisters,
way over here, to, uhh,

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:48.200
"Shoot for the moon.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.167
You might land
amongst the stars."

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:51.567
[ Laughter and applause ]
And then, finally,

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.367
my older brother David,
way over here, is,

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:55.133
"If you want a rainbow,
you're going to have

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:56.767
to put up with some rain."

00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:59.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:03.501
There are now five kids
simultaneously throwing up

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:05.567
into one pool,
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.567 --> 00:06:08.033
which is way too many kids.

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:10.033
I know that because the
other rich parents

00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:12.834
are now freaking out.

00:06:12.834 --> 00:06:18.133
Because we are all
so far spread out in the pool,

00:06:18.133 --> 00:06:20.801
it doesn't look like
some isolated incident.

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:22.334
[ Laughter ]
In their minds,

00:06:22.334 --> 00:06:25.701
it looks like some sort
of violent super virus

00:06:25.701 --> 00:06:30.767
has swept over the entire pool,
causing kids to explode.

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:31.968
Kids are screaming.

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:34.501
Parents are pulling their kids
out by the arms.

00:06:34.501 --> 00:06:36.701
There's kids throwing up
that didn't even eat

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:38.133
trash bags of ice cream.

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:41.567
I get out of the pool.

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.701
The pool is ruined.

00:06:43.701 --> 00:06:44.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.767 --> 00:06:48.434
And I remember
just thinking to myself,

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:50.133
"Man.

00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:52.100
This place needs
better security."

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:56.000
So this has been one
of the better birthdays.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.234
[ Cheering ]
Thank you so much!

00:06:57.234 --> 00:06:59.501
You've been great.
Oh!

00:06:59.501 --> 00:07:00.901
♪♪

00:07:00.901 --> 00:07:03.200
-How are you doing?

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.567
Happy Birthday, buddy.

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:05.601
What a treat!

00:07:05.601 --> 00:07:06.968
That is how you do it,
right there.

00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:09.467
That's Moses Storm.

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:12.467
"Trash White"
is streaming now on HBO Max.

